
§ diff


- diff (1)
	° compare files line by line 

- symbols and their meaning

	° ---: Marks the beginning of the section representing the original contents of the first file (often referred to as the "old" file or the "original" file).

	° +++: Marks the beginning of the section representing the modified contents of the second file (often referred to as the "new" file or the "modified" file).

	° <:   Indicates that the line appears only in the first file (old file) and has been removed in the second file (new file).

	° >:   Indicates that the line appears only in the second file (new file) and has been added or modified from the first file (old file).

	° |:   Separates sections of context lines from the actual changes
               Context lines are lines that remain unchanged between the two files but provide context around the changes.

	° !:   Indicates that the line has been changed in both files but with conflicting changes.
               This typically appears in unified diff format and highlights merge conflicts.




